{
  "description": "#5281 — the per-space tag-name rule of #5236 holds on rename and restore too: a second live tag under one normalized name is the one the tags cache drops, so it vanishes from the Tags view, the `#` picker, `tag:#` search and the tag filters while its blocks keep the chip. The ops make a space (`C1`) and three tags in it (`meeting` C2, `notes` C3, `standup` C4) through the commands, so each tag carries its space on both stacks. Renaming `notes` to `Meeting`, a case variant `normalize_tag_name` folds onto C2's name, is refused with `DuplicatePageTitle` and writes nothing. Once C2 is trashed its name is free, and the same rename (to `meeting`) goes through. Restoring C2 now would put two live `meeting` tags in the space, so the batch that lists it is refused whole: C4, listed beside it, stays in the trash too, and neither refusal appends an op.",
